<p>President Trump said the United States could end its military campaign in Iran within two to three weeks, adding that a withdrawal would not necessarily depend on Tehran reaching a deal with Washington. The White House later said he would address the nation on Wednesday evening with an update on Iran, underscoring that the month-old conflict may be moving into a new phase. The comments came as the war entered its fifth week, with U.S. officials still describing sustained military pressure on Iran while also signaling a possible endgame. Multiple reports said the fighting has rattled energy markets and pushed average U.S. gasoline prices above $4 a gallon, while the closure of the Strait of Hormuz remained a central source of international tension. Even with those pressures, some officials said they could see a path to ending the fighting — a small sign that diplomacy and military pressure may be converging toward a conclusion.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Juy2vuTwR05feaLpWZhafJ7eS5OFVcSfS6Ziws6_W4SLEu10hh6neGp9fvxGFaidHSGUDRmrreWHNOWMu2MDSdihLzIImAvWKSWUQGJCndqodHo-bfX8sJLNZVVjszQ-AM0pDAYQyjAsNP6QgNFaP9Nmp0MYq8T_fWrwPt7bzdLwW_jBQrp0jy--5K8AbFfC5NPWi45Evp2Nuw' alt='President Trump told reporters on Tuesday that he had attained his goal of dealing with Iran’s nuclear program and that gasoline prices in the United States would be coming down.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Washington&#x27;s mixed signals: Politico reported that Pentagon officials earlier on Tuesday had been careful not to set any timeline for ending the campaign, even as Trump later said the U.S. could leave in two to three weeks, highlighting uneven public messaging about how the war might end.</li><li>Allies pressure: Trump said countries that rely on the Strait of Hormuz should take responsibility for reopening it, with PBS and Al Jazeera quoting him telling allies to &quot;get your own oil&quot;.</li><li>NATO signal: Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Washington would have to &quot;reexamine&quot; its relationship with NATO after the conflict, linking the Iran war to broader tensions within the alliance.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: Trump said the United States would leave once it judged Iran unable to develop a nuclear weapon, framing withdrawal around that military objective rather than a formal diplomatic deal. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/01/trump-says-us-to-leave-iran-very-soon-deal-or-not-we-re-finishing-the-job_6751999_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>Iran&#x27;s foreign minister: Iran&#x27;s top diplomat told Al Jazeera there was &quot;no truth&quot; to claims of active U.S.-Iran negotiations, directly challenging U.S. assertions that talks were underway. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/31/no-truth-to-us-iranian-negotiations-irans-fm-tells-al-jazeera'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Marco Rubio: Rubio said Washington could see the war&#x27;s &quot;finish line,&quot; signaling that senior U.S. officials believe the campaign is moving toward a close rather than toward open-ended escalation. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/rubio-says-us-can-see-finish-line-iran-war'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Pete Hegseth: At a public briefing, Hegseth said Iran still had the capacity to strike back even after weeks of U.S.-Israeli bombardment, while insisting Tehran&#x27;s military power had been severely degraded. (<a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-31-0700/middle-east-iran-war-live-updates-trump-says-us-could-leave-2-3-weeks'>AllSides</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-trump-says-us-will-be-leaving-soon/live-76615254'>Iran war: Trump says US will be &#x27;leaving soon&#x27;</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/31/world/iran-war-oil-trump'>Trump Says U.S. Military Campaign to Wind Down and Plans National Address</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldn